(C) The plaintiff’s injuries from the vehicle collision were due to defendant’s negligent driving.

Code pleading never became a part of federal civil procedure, but the state courts’ experiences with code pleading were influential in the efforts of the drafters of the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure (“Rules”), which were created to replace the common law and equity procedure then employed by the federal courts.

In the 1800s, reform movements led some state courts (but not the federal courts) to replace common law pleading with “code pleading”

•Code pleading eliminated the forms of actions and relied on pleading of “facts constituting the cause of action”
